<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balian of Arsuf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1277</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Balian of Ibelin, lord of Arsuf</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsuf">Arsuf</a> was a thirteenth-century baron of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-ibelin">Ibelin family</a>, son of John of Ibelin, lord of Arsuf. He served as bailli, or regent, of the kingdom. Burdened by debts and the cost of defence, he leased Arsuf to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> in 1261, four years before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> captured and destroyed the town.</p></div>
